    s.push(e("worker.compactBeforeFix", "Compact before a fix round", Work, Ty::Switch, json!(false), "before a fix round (a review that sent the work back), the working agent is told to compact its conversation, keeping the issue, the branch and files changed, what was traced, the last check and open questions, and dropping file dumps and finished searches; the findings go to it once the compact is over. Claude only. A compact that fails still sends the findings. runner.log says `fix round 1: compacted (before 180000 tokens)`"));
    s.extend(role("reviewer", "the reviewer", "codex", true, Work));
    s.push(e("reviewer.fallback", "Reviewer's fallback", Work, Ty::Agents, json!("none"), "who takes over when the reviewer cannot go on: a list of agents tried in order (`codex, claude/claude-opus-5-5`; a model after a slash, as in `reviewer.agent`), or `none`. It reviews in its place when the reviewer's provider is down (after the board's own tries), the reviewer is out of allowance or logged out, or its program is not installed here; it then reviews the later rounds of that task too. With the list used up the review fails as before. Nobody extra runs until then. More: [the fallback agent](fallback.md)"));
    s.push(e("reviewer.byLabel", "Reviewer by issue label", Work, Ty::List, json!("none"), "issue labels (`kind:docs, kind:chore`) whose tasks the first usable agent on `reviewer.fallback` reviews instead of `reviewer.agent`, every round, on its own effort. The issue is the one the task's description names (\"Implements GitHub issue owner/repo#n (…/issues/n)\"); its labels are asked of gh when each review starts. With no issue, none of these labels, or gh failing, `reviewer.agent` reviews; so does it when the routed reviewer is cut off and nobody usable is left on the list. Each review's reviewer and why is said in the task's runner.log"));
    s.push(e("reviewer.codexPace", "Codex paced by its allowance", Work, Ty::List, json!("none"), "issue labels (`kind:faithful, kind:bug`) whose tasks Codex (`reviewer.agent`, when it is codex) reviews while its weekly allowance used is under the share of the week gone by, plus 5 points, and the first usable agent on `reviewer.fallback` reviews otherwise, every round. The reading is Codex's own (its session files' rate limits); one over an hour old sends one review to Codex to refresh it. A `reviewer.byLabel` label routes first. Each review's reviewer and why (`pace: used 30% < elapsed 42% + 5`) is said in the task's runner.log"));
    s.push(e("reviewer.claudeModelByLabel", "Claude reviewer's model by label", Work, Ty::List, json!("none"), "`label=model` pairs (`kind:docs=sonnet`): when Claude reviews a task whose issue has one of those labels, it reviews on that model, every round; the first pair whose label the issue has wins. Who reviews is decided first (`reviewer.byLabel`, `reviewer.codexPace`, `reviewer.laterAgent`). With no issue or none of these labels, the reviewer's own model. runner.log says `review 1: reviewer claude sonnet (kind:docs)`"));
    s.push(e("reviewer.laterAgent", "Reviewer from round 2", Work, Ty::Agent, json!("same"), "who reviews a task from its second review round on: `fallback` for the first usable agent on `reviewer.fallback`, a program (with an optional model after a slash, as in `reviewer.agent`), or `same` for no change. It reviews on its own effort. A `reviewer.byLabel` label still routes first. When it is cut off with nobody usable left, `reviewer.agent` reviews that round, and the next round tries it again. Each review's reviewer and why (`round 2+`) is said in the task's runner.log"));
