    s.push(e("review.timeout", "Review may run for", Work, Ty::Time, json!("20m"), "how long one review may take, and one comparison of attempts: a time (`45m`, `1h`) or `none`. Read when the review starts. Reached: the reviewer is stopped and the review fails (`review timed out after 20m (review.timeout)`), and what happens next is as for any failed review. Not from the repo's own file, so the code under review cannot change it. Unlike `limit.time`, which stops any run and waits for you. More: [the gate](gate.md)").none().means("how long one review may take. At it the review fails, as any failed review. Read when the review starts"));
